[[Skeleton]]s are [[undead]] [[monster]]s that can be assigned as tasks at combat level 15 by various low-level Slayer masters. They are often found in cemeteries and dungeons. A good strategy to kill them is to use melee with a weapon with [[Crush weapons|crush]] bonuses (such as a [[Viggora's chainmace]]) and a [[salve amulet]] or [[salve amulet (e)]], due to their low crush defence.

Another strategy to kill them would be with magic. Many skeletons have an [[elemental weakness]] to [[earth spells]], making those a very effective option.

Players who seek a greater challenge can choose to kill [[Vet'ion]] or [[Calvar'ion]]. These bosses are significantly stronger than the typical skeleton, but provide plenty of rewards for players who seek to kill them. In order to access Calvar'ion, the player must have completed the [[Wilderness Diary#Hard|Hard Wilderness Diary]]. Vet'ion only requires completing the [[Wilderness Diary#Medium|Medium Wilderness Diary]], but is deeper in the Wilderness and resides in a [[multicombat area]]. Accessing the bosses requires a one-time payment of {{NoCoins|50000}} coins, which must be repaid again if the player dies to another player in the Wilderness. Note that the skeletal hellhounds they summon also count towards the task, so every kill at the boss is equal to five skeletons per spawn.

If players are not seeking to kill either skeleton boss but are assigned them in the Wilderness, an ideal location would be the [[Edgeville Dungeon]], as there is a good cluster of skeletons that can be easily cannoned and has a quick escape, provided that the player is paying attention.

